# Generated and per-machine. Nothing in here is source.
#
# Persistent sandbox state — the account's live OAuth credential, prompt
# history, session transcripts, the ~224MB Claude Code binaries — is not
# here to ignore: it lives in $CABOOSE_DATA_DIR, by default under
# ~/.caboose, outside this checkout on purpose. A tracked .gitignore cannot
# protect live state — checking out a commit that predates the file
# un-ignores everything it covered, and the next snapshot takes it.
#
# The sandbox's own CLAUDE.md is tracked at sandbox/CLAUDE.md and copied into
# the data dir's .claude/ by the launcher on every start.

# Claude Code worktree scratch space, created inside whatever checkout it is
# working in. Empty here today; a `git add -A` must not start tracking it.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The launcher, built from cmd/caboose by `make launcher`. It sits at the repo
# root, where PATH symlinks and the Makefile expect it, but it is build output.
# caboose.platform records the GOOS/GOARCH it was built for, so a binary from
# another platform (the sandbox shares this checkout) gets rebuilt.
/caboose
/caboose.platform

# The version the launcher was stamped with at its last `make launcher`,
# recorded next to caboose.platform so a binary with a stale stamp gets rebuilt.
/caboose.version

# goreleaser's output: the release archives and checksums
# from `goreleaser release` (or a `--snapshot` dry run). Build output only.
/dist/

# caboose-agent for each architecture, from `make agent`, embedded in the
# launcher. Build output; agent-bin/README.md is the one tracked file.
/agent-bin/caboose-agent-*
